From 0000000000000000000000000000000000000000 Mon Sep 17 00:00:00 2001
From: Ondrej Jirman <megi@xff.cz>
Date: Thu, 6 Aug 2026 21:50:23 +0200
Subject: media: sun6i-isp: Let the demosaic minimums be set apart

The demosaic's minimum RGB occupies three separate ten bit fields
across two registers. Every caller that has ever been seen writes the
same value into all three -- the vendor library does it in one function,
and this driver copied that -- so whether the three do different things
has never been tested.

Give each field its own value in the parameters, and while here let
CFA_TEX be written too. That register is one the hardware writes its own
measurement into; nothing is known to write it, and this is how to find
out whether writing has any effect.

Setting all three minimums alike reproduces the previous behaviour.

Signed-off-by: Ondrej Jirman <megi@xff.cz>
---
 drivers/staging/media/sunxi/sun6i-isp/sun6i_isp_params.c      | 16 ++++-
 drivers/staging/media/sunxi/sun6i-isp/uapi/sun6i-isp-config.h | 33 +++++++++-
 2 files changed, 45 insertions(+), 4 deletions(-)

diff --git a/drivers/staging/media/sunxi/sun6i-isp/sun6i_isp_params.c b/drivers/staging/media/sunxi/sun6i-isp/sun6i_isp_params.c
index 111111111111..222222222222 100644
--- a/drivers/staging/media/sunxi/sun6i-isp/sun6i_isp_params.c
+++ b/drivers/staging/media/sunxi/sun6i-isp/sun6i_isp_params.c
@@ -446,10 +446,20 @@ sun6i_isp_params_configure_cfa(struct sun6i_isp_device *isp_dev,
 			     SUN6I_ISP_CFA_CFG0_DIR_TH(cfa->direction_threshold) |
 			     SUN6I_ISP_CFA_CFG0_MIN_RGB(cfa->min_rgb));
 
-	/* the same minimum again, in both halves of the second register */
+	/*
+	 * The other two copies of the minimum, which every caller so far has
+	 * set to the same value as the first. They are separate here so that
+	 * assumption can be tested rather than inherited.
+	 */
 	sun6i_isp_load_write(isp_dev, SUN6I_ISP_CFA_CFG1_REG,
-			     SUN6I_ISP_CFA_CFG1_MIN_RGB_LOW(cfa->min_rgb) |
-			     SUN6I_ISP_CFA_CFG1_MIN_RGB_HIGH(cfa->min_rgb));
+			     SUN6I_ISP_CFA_CFG1_MIN_RGB_LOW(cfa->min_rgb_low) |
+			     SUN6I_ISP_CFA_CFG1_MIN_RGB_HIGH(cfa->min_rgb_high));
+
+	/*
+	 * A register the hardware writes its own measurement into. Writing it
+	 * may do nothing at all; that is what this is for.
+	 */
+	sun6i_isp_load_write(isp_dev, SUN6I_ISP_CFA_TEX_REG, cfa->texture);
 }
 
 /*
diff --git a/drivers/staging/media/sunxi/sun6i-isp/uapi/sun6i-isp-config.h b/drivers/staging/media/sunxi/sun6i-isp/uapi/sun6i-isp-config.h
index 111111111111..222222222222 100644
--- a/drivers/staging/media/sunxi/sun6i-isp/uapi/sun6i-isp-config.h
+++ b/drivers/staging/media/sunxi/sun6i-isp/uapi/sun6i-isp-config.h
@@ -245,10 +245,23 @@ struct sun6i_isp_params_config_dpc {
  * to an edge direction; the minimum is a floor applied to the channels,
  * and the hardware writes its own measurement back over the same bits, so
  * reading these registers returns a level rather than what was written.
+ *
+ * The minimum occupies three separate 10-bit fields across two registers.
+ * Every caller that has ever been seen -- the vendor library and this
+ * driver before it -- writes the same value into all three, so whether
+ * they do different things has never been tested. They are separate here
+ * so that it can be. Set all three alike for the vendor's behaviour.
+ *
+ * texture goes to CFA_TEX. That register is a measurement the hardware
+ * writes back; nothing is known to read it and nothing is known to write
+ * it, so this exists to find out whether writing has any effect at all.
  */
 struct sun6i_isp_params_config_cfa {
 	__u16	direction_threshold;
-	__u16	min_rgb;
+	__u16	min_rgb;		/* CFA_CFG0, bits 25:16 */
+	__u16	min_rgb_low;		/* CFA_CFG1, bits 9:0 */
+	__u16	min_rgb_high;		/* CFA_CFG1, bits 25:16 */
+	__u32	texture;		/* CFA_TEX */
 };
 
 /*
@@ -310,6 +323,7 @@ struct sun6i_isp_params_config {
 #define SUN6I_ISP_STAT_AF			(1U << 2)
 #define SUN6I_ISP_STAT_AFS			(1U << 3)
 #define SUN6I_ISP_STAT_AWB			(1U << 4)
+#define SUN6I_ISP_STAT_CFA			(1U << 5)
 
 /*
  * 128 bins over a 256 level range, so bin i covers luminance 2 * i + 1.
@@ -392,6 +406,22 @@ struct sun6i_isp_stats_awb {
  * the rest are left zeroed. The sum ordering is believed to be red,
  * green, blue.
  */
+/*
+ * What the demosaic measured, taken from the save region rather than from
+ * the statistics DMA -- the hardware reports these by writing back over
+ * its own configuration registers.
+ *
+ * min_rgb is the minimum the block saw, which the vendor's 3A loop reads
+ * every frame. texture is the whole of CFA_TEX; the vendor exports a
+ * getter for it and never calls it, so what it counts is not known.
+ *
+ * The demosaic has no enable bit, so these are always reported.
+ */
+struct sun6i_isp_stats_cfa {
+	__u32				min_rgb;
+	__u32				texture;
+};
+
 struct sun6i_isp_stats_buffer {
 	__u32				blocks_valid;
 	__u32				sequence;
@@ -401,6 +431,7 @@ struct sun6i_isp_stats_buffer {
 	struct sun6i_isp_stats_af	af;
 	struct sun6i_isp_stats_afs	afs;
 	struct sun6i_isp_stats_awb	awb;
+	struct sun6i_isp_stats_cfa	cfa;
 };
 
 #endif /* _UAPI_SUN6I_ISP_CONFIG_H */
-- 
Armbian

